# Level 29, reached by password, then the ice weapon carried across the whole map
# to the one creature in the game the corpus can freeze.
#
# This is `movies/level5-d7f6.zmv`'s other half. `enemy_d7f6_collide` had six
# untaken branches; that movie took three of them with the squirt gun, and the
# only one left with an input at all is `d7f6_special`, the `CMP #$005D : BEQ`
# that hands the creature to `$81:847E`. It wants the ice weapon and a
# `$81:D704` actor **on the same level**, and exactly one level a password
# reaches has both:
#
#   level 5   creature open, ice weapon sealed in a basement pocket (667,1068)
#   level 17  ice weapon open, creature sealed in an alcove (563,513)
#   level 31  both, no password
#   level 29  both --- this movie
#
# `zamn_assets route ... --reach` is what says "sealed" rather than "far".
#
# The route is 2,800 frames long and was fitted in four goes, because level 29 is
# a maze and `tools/fit_route.py` had one fixed unstick step:
#
#   2560 -> 3672   spawn (277,1435) to the type $02 object at (756,730)
#   3730 -> 4325   south loop out of the cul-de-sac, up to (773,461)
#   4370 -> 4610   hand-walked: Left to the wall at x=721, then Down to y=591
#   4620 -> 5344   (721,591) to (203,241), 27 legs
#
# The third leg is the interesting one. At (773,461) the way west is a 56-pixel
# detour south, and the fitter spent 41 legs stepping 28 pixels down, 28 back up
# and asking the same blocked question again -- one nudge length cannot clear a
# chicane. Walking on to the wall at (721,591) by hand cut the remaining route
# from 277 cells to 147 and it fitted first time. `STUCK_NUDGE` is `(14, 28, 56)`
# now, which is the same fix without the hand-walking.
#
# Two things the object needed:
#
#   * **It is on a blocked cell.** (756,730) has no route to it and every cell
#     around it does; the player stands at x=751 and the game's eight-pixel touch
#     box does the rest. `--watch 1CCE` says it worked: $0000 -> $0099 at 3679.
#   * **B is pressed at 5390 and not earlier**, which is 1,700 frames after the
#     pickup rather than the 460 the lockout needs -- the walk pays for it.
#     `$7E:1CBC` goes $0000 -> $0001 at 5392 and stays there.
#
# The fight is a retreat, not a stand: this creature chases, so the player walks
# west with Y held and it follows. Every shot on screen reads `$5D` -- 69 of them
# in 200 sampled frames, against no other weapon-range id at all.
#
# What it buys: `d7f6_special` 5, and `freeze_took`, `freeze_counting` and
# `freeze_already` off a ninth caller.
#
